                      <speaker value="HUMAN" />
                      <text value="In Elm, is there a better way to repeat this view 3 times?" />
                    </message>
                    <message>
                      <speaker value="ASSISTANT" />
                      <text value="Yes, there is a more idiomatic way to repeat a view a certain number of times in Elm. Instead of using `List.map` with `List.range`, you can use the `List.repeat` function, which creates a list with a given length, where all elements are the same value.&#10;&#10;Here's how you can rewrite the code:&#10;&#10;```elm&#10;List.repeat numAvailableSlots availableRelicView&#10;```&#10;&#10;This will create a list with `numAvailableSlots` elements, where each element is the `availableRelicView` value.&#10;&#10;The `List.repeat` function is more concise and easier to read than using `List.map` with `List.range`. It also avoids the unnecessary lambda function `\_ -&gt;`." />
                    </message>
                  </list>
